target/
*.png

# Basemaps and derived data — rebuildable from scripts/, and large. Excluded
# per-file rather than as a directory: `data/` would exclude the directory
# itself, and git cannot re-include anything under a directory it has excluded,
# which silently drops the tour sheet below.
data/*
!data/places.txt

# The building footprints, and the reason they are the second exception.
#
# Everything else under data/ is a basemap that any machine can rebuild and
# that no deployment reads from git -- the 1.7 GB PMTiles archive is mounted,
# not committed. This one is different in every way that matters: three
# megabytes, generated once from the tour's own stops, and the *only* source of
# buildings there is, because the vector archive has no buildings layer at all.
#
# Left ignored it never reached production. The Dockerfile copies map data by
# name and this was not one of the names, so the extrusion built into the
# renderer -- Mode::Half3D, Mode::Full3D, the whole tilt ramp -- had never once
# had anything to draw for a visitor.
!data/buildings.tmap
